Report payload strictness:
- The `submit_report` payload uses a strict schema: any field not listed in the
  tool input schema is rejected (`extra="forbid"`). Read the tool's parameter
  schema as the source of truth.
- Required top-level keys: `cover` (object) and `sections` (non-empty array).
  Do NOT submit `cover: {}` — Cover requires `title` (string), `subtitle`
  (string), and `tagline` (string). Optional: `eyebrow`, `ticker`, `tldr`
  (list of short strings), `tldr_label`, `key_metrics`. The framework you are
  handed has a `cover.instructions` field telling you what to write into each
  cover field — read it and populate every required field.
- Each entry in `sections` requires `id` (snake_case string), `title`
  (string), and `blocks` (non-empty list). Use the framework's
  `section.instructions` to decide block content.
- Do NOT emit `page_furniture`, `schema_version`, `department`, or
  `generated_at`. The server fills these.
- Do NOT copy framework-only scaffolding fields (`instructions`, null
  placeholders) into the submitted payload — the schema rejects unknown keys.
- Chart blocks (line_chart, bar_chart, area_chart, pie_chart,
  candlestick_chart, waterfall_chart, scatter_plot, heatmap, treemap,
  combo_chart) accept `options` with ONLY three keys:
  `{height, show_legend, show_grid}`. No `note`, no `caption`, no `subtitle`
  inside options — put commentary in the chart `title` or an adjacent
  `text` block.
- `combo_chart.bar_series` and `combo_chart.line_series` items must be shaped
  `{"name": str, "values": [float, ...]}` (one value per `categories` entry).
  Do NOT use `data` for these series — that key is reserved for
  line_chart/area_chart/scatter_plot, whose series carry `{x, y}` points.
  Example: `"bar_series": [{"name": "Revenue", "values": [3.2, 5.0, 7.2]}]`.
- Table `headers` must be a list of objects shaped `{key, label}` (with
  optional `align`, `sortable`, `sparkline`). Plain strings are rejected.
  Example: `[{"key": "ticker", "label": "Ticker"}, {"key": "price", "label": "Price", "align": "right"}]`.
- Metric `value` and `delta` must be strings. Numeric inputs (e.g., `0.123`)
  are rejected — format as `"12.3%"` or `"$1.23"`.
- `rail.sparkline.points` must be a list of objects shaped `{"x": float, "y": float}`
  (min 2 points). Flat numeric arrays like `[120.5, 121.2]` and bare pairs
  like `[[1, 120.5], [2, 121.2]]` are rejected.
  Example: `[{"x": 0, "y": 120.5}, {"x": 1, "y": 121.2}, {"x": 2, "y": 119.8}]`.
- If validation fails, you will receive the error list as a `submit_report`
  tool result. Fix every listed field and call `submit_report` again with
  the corrected payload.
